From 0db5afe715ae6e3299da8722cd8f38e5ff9aefd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:12:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] devices: a TPM 2.0 over TIS MMIO, run by a host backend

MacNeutron's microVM will need a TPM 2.0 for anti-cheat that asks for one.
TpmDevice (krun_tpm_device_new, libkrun_tpm.h) puts a TPM behind the TCG PC
Client TIS (FIFO) interface: five 4 KiB localities of MMIO and a device-tree
node, "tcg,tpm-tis-mmio", which Linux's built-in tpm_tis binds to and polls
(no interrupt is offered). The host's backend, a C vtable, runs each command
on a thread of its own, so a slow one doesn't stall the vCPU that started it;
a failed one answers TPM_RC_FAILURE.

AttachContext::register_platform puts a non-virtio MMIO device on the bus with
a device-tree node (macOS, aarch64).
